<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50127" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vălesco</span></b> , ĕre,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
			n.</i> [valeo], <i>to grow strong</i>, <i>acquire strength</i> (rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic.): (puerorum aetas) tali pacto
					recreata valescat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					1, 942</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 17</span></i>: sucus
			ex quo omne corpus valescit, Ambros. de Noë et Arca, 9,
			28.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scelera impetu, bona consilia mora valescere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					1, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">falsa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					2, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superstitiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meditatio et labor in posterum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 61</span></i>
			.</div>
